  "firstStarterQuestion": "Which service agents have the highest number of unresolved service requests assigned?",
  "secondStarterQuestion": "What are the 5 most common issues reported across all service requests?",
  "thirdStarterQuestion": "Which service requests are currently overdue or at risk of breaching their SLA?",
  "followupEnabledFlag": false,
  "followupPrompt": "Based on the most recent conversation in $param.system_context.chat_history, generate $param.system_context.number_of_follow_up_questions follow-up questions.\nEach follow-up question must relate directly to the specific topics, entities, or record identifiers (such as service request numbers) just presented in the user's prior results. Use all record numbers, IDs, names, or codes exactly as shown in the latest output; do not change the format, add extra characters, or insert additional symbols (e.g., do not add hyphens or spaces to SR numbers).\n\nStrictly adhere to the JSON Schema format below and do not include any explanations, formatting instructions, or additional text.\n\nJSON Schema:\n[{\"question\": \"\"}, {\"question\": \"\"}, {\"question\": \"\"}]\n\n--ANSWER REQUIREMENTS--\n\nUse only content from $param.system_context.chat_history to construct the follow-up questions.\nGenerate the exact number of questions indicated in $param.system_context.number_of_follow_up_questions.\nEach question must reference entities, SR numbers, records, or fields as they appear in the latest system output—without extra characters, changes, or formatting adjustments.\nFollow-up questions should be highly relevant, actionable, and encourage further exploration, drill-down, or resolution steps related to the visible results. (e.g., \"Would you like to view resolution details for SR292483?\" not \"SR-292483\").\nThe output must contain only the valid JSON array as specified.\n--ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS--\n\nDo not include any extra text, explanations, or formatting outside the JSON array.\nKeep questions concise, natural, and focused on the user's last set of results.\nNever alter or reformat record numbers, IDs, codes, or other key references when constructing questions.\nDo not provide reminders, closing statements, or references to system processes.",
